Release Notes for version 2.0-9
-------------------------------

o  As pointed out by Avril Coghlan on the seqinR diffusion list on
    17-MAR-2010 there was a bug in the getAnnot() function.
    This is now fixed.

o  As suggested by Avril Coghlan on the seqinR diffusion list on
    02-MAR-2010 the function rho() has gained a wordsize
    argument.

o  The argument word in function count() is
    now more explicitely called wordsize.

o  The example section in file read.alignment.Rd has gained
    a new quality control sanity check.

o  The File argument that was deprecated since seqinR
    release 1.1-3 in function read.alignment() is no more valid.
    Just use file instead.

o  As pointed by Darren Obbard on the seqinr diffusion list on
    05-MAR-2010 there was a memory leak problem when calling the
    read.alignment() function with the fasta format. This
    is now fixed for the fasta format, but the remaining formats have
    not been checked for this problem.


